IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- K2-art-2b.l4 -- ARTICLE 2(3) AND (4) OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679 (layer 1).
-- Written by K2 (Sonnet 5.5).  Lines 27-28 of eu-gdpr-2016-679-consolidated-20160504.txt.
-- Article 2(1) and (2) (material scope, lines 21-26) are P1's: this module takes P1's answer to them as an
-- input where it needs it (K2-art-3.l4), and does not repeat them.
-- Target compiler: main (build 1.6.112).  Answers: MAYBE BOOLEAN.  JUST FALSE only where the text says no;
-- NOTHING where it does not (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled).
--
-- WHAT THESE TWO PARAGRAPHS MEAN TO A PERSON.  A person whose personal data are processed by a Union
-- institution, body, office or agency looks to Regulation (EC) No 45/2001, which Art 2(3) names, and not to
-- this Regulation (reading A, fork FK2-1: the brief's reading, which the text states only by naming the
-- other instrument).  A person who relies on, or is liable under, Directive 2000/31/EC, in particular its
-- rules on the liability of intermediary service providers, finds that this Regulation leaves them in place
-- (Art 2(4)).  The second sentence of Art 2(3) is a duty of the Union's lawmakers that names no party
-- (fork FK2-2): it is a decision function only.
-- ============================================================================

§ `Article 2(3): processing by the Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies`

-- src:27 | 3. For the processing of personal data by the Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies, Regulation (EC) No 45/2001 applies. Regulation (EC) No 45/2001 and other Union legal acts applicable to such processing of personal data shall be adapted to the principles and rules of this Regulation in accordance with Article 98.
@ref Art 2(3) first sentence: Regulation (EC) No 45/2001 applies (src:27)
GIVEN `the processing is by the Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(3) Regulation (EC) No 45/2001 applies to the processing, where it is by the Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies` MEANS
    IF `the processing is by the Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is "For the processing of personal data by the Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies"; for processing by anyone else it says nothing of Regulation (EC) No 45/2001
    -- Whether Regulation (EC) No 45/2001 is still the instrument that applies is a fact outside the sources and is not decided here (NOTES: Open questions).

-- Reading A (the brief's, fork FK2-1): the sentence names another instrument as the one that applies, and for
-- the processing of those bodies this Regulation does not.  The text says it only by naming the other
-- instrument, so the JUST FALSE below is a marginal reading, listed for a lawyer (NOTES: Marginal readings).
-- src:27 | 3. For the processing of personal data by the Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies, Regulation (EC) No 45/2001 applies. Regulation (EC) No 45/2001 and other Union legal acts applicable to such processing of personal data shall be adapted to the principles and rules of this Regulation in accordance with Article 98.
@ref Art 2(3) first sentence: this Regulation does not govern that processing (src:27)
GIVEN `the processing is by the Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(3) this Regulation applies to the processing, where it is by the Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies` MEANS
    IF `the processing is by the Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (marginal reading FK2-1, the text says no only by naming another instrument): "For the processing of personal data by the Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies, Regulation (EC) No 45/2001 applies."
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about processing "by the Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies"; for any other processing it does not say whether this Regulation applies

-- The second sentence is a duty in the passive that names no party (fork FK2-2): a decision function only,
-- no regulative rule.  The words "applicable to such processing" are a scope limit with no gate word, so an act that
-- is not applicable to it is outside the sentence (NOTHING, periods ruling (c)).
-- src:27 | 3. For the processing of personal data by the Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies, Regulation (EC) No 45/2001 applies. Regulation (EC) No 45/2001 and other Union legal acts applicable to such processing of personal data shall be adapted to the principles and rules of this Regulation in accordance with Article 98.
@ref Art 2(3) second sentence: adaptation of the Union legal acts (src:27)
GIVEN `the Union legal act is applicable to the processing of personal data by the Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act has been adapted to the principles and rules of this Regulation in accordance with Article 98` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(3) the Union legal act applicable to such processing is adapted to the principles and rules of this Regulation in accordance with Article 98` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the Union legal act is applicable to the processing of personal data by the Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "Regulation (EC) No 45/2001 and other Union legal acts applicable to such processing of personal data"
        IF `the act has been adapted to the principles and rules of this Regulation in accordance with Article 98`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "shall be adapted to the principles and rules of this Regulation in accordance with Article 98"

§ `Article 2(4): without prejudice to Directive 2000/31/EC`

-- src:28 | 4. This Regulation shall be without prejudice to the application of Directive 2000/31/EC, in particular of the liability rules of intermediary service providers in Articles 12 to 15 of that Directive.
@ref Art 2(4) without prejudice to Directive 2000/31/EC (src:28)
GIVEN `the matter is the application of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is the liability rules of intermediary service providers in Articles 12 to 15 of that Directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(4) this Regulation is without prejudice to the application of Directive 2000/31/EC` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the application of Directive 2000/31/EC` OR `the matter is the liability rules of intermediary service providers in Articles 12 to 15 of that Directive`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- JUST TRUE is the text's own no to any prejudice, a flat negative: "This Regulation shall be without prejudice to the application of Directive 2000/31/EC".
    -- "in particular of the liability rules of intermediary service providers in Articles 12 to 15 of that Directive": the liability rules are an instance of the application of the Directive, so either input brings the answer.
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provision saves only "the application of Directive 2000/31/EC"; for any other instrument it does not say whether this Regulation is without prejudice to it
